      "text": "We notice that $x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n} = \\frac{x^{2^{n + 1}} - 1}{x^{2^n}}.$ Therefore,\n\\[\\frac{1}{x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}} = \\frac{x^{2^n}}{x^{2^{n + 1}} - 1}.\\]Then\n\\begin{align*}\n\\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{1}{x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}} &= \\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{x^{2^n}}{x^{2^{n + 1}} - 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{x^{2^0} - 1} + \\frac{x^8}{x^4 - 1} + \\frac{x^{16}}{x^8 - 1} + \\frac{x^{32}}{x^{16} - 1} + \\dotsb \\\\\n&= 1 + \\frac{1}{1 - x^4} + \\frac{1}{1 - x^8} + \\frac{1}{1 - x^{16}} + \\frac{1}{1 - x^{32}} + \\dotsb \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{1 - x^4} + \\frac{1}{1 - x^8} + \\frac{1}{1 - x^{16}} + \\frac{1}{1 - x^{32}} + \\dotsb \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\left(1 - x^4\\right)\\left(1 + x^4 + x^8 + x^{16} + x^{32} + \\dotsb\\right)}.\n\\end{align*}Thus, the desired sum is $\\boxed{\\frac{1}{(1 - x^4)(1 + x^4 + x^8 + x^{16} + x^{32} + \\dotsb)}}.$The answer is: \\frac{1}{(1-x^4)(1+x^4+x^8+x^{16}+x^{32}+\\dotsb)}",
