      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "By the formula for finite geometric series, we have\n\\[S = \\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{1}{x^{2^n} - (x^{-2^n})} = \\sum_{n= 0}^\\infty \\frac{1}{x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}} = \\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{1}{x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}} \\cdot \\frac{x^{2^{n + 1}}}{x^{2^{n+1}}}. \\]\nWe find that $\\dfrac{x^{2^{n + 1}}}{x^{2^n}} = x^{2^n + 2^n} = x^{2^{n+1}}$, so our computation simplifies to\n\\[ \\begin{aligned} S &= \\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{x^{2^{n + 1}}}{x^{2^{n + 1}} - x^{-2^{n + 1}}} \\\\ &= \\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{x^{2^{n + 1}}}{x^{2^n} \\left( x^{2^{n + 1}} - x^{-2^{n + 1}}\\right)} \\\\ &= \\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{x^{2^n}}{1 - x^{-2^{n + 1}}} \\\\ &= \\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{x^{2^n}}{x^{-2^{n + 1}} - 1}. \\end{aligned} \\]\nSince $x > 1$, we know that $x^{-2^{n + 1}} < 1$ for all $n$.  Multiplying both sides of the inequality by $x^{2^n}$, we get\n\\[ \\frac{x^{2^n}}{x^{-2^{n + 1}} - 1} < x^{2^n + 2^n}. \\]\nThus, when we sum from $0$ to $\\infty$, we get\n\\[ \\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{x^{2^n}}{x^{-2^{n + 1}} - 1} > \\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty x^{2^n + 2^n}. \\]\nThe right side telescopes, so the inequality holds. $\\blacksquare$\n\nThe answer is: 1",
